3. ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS (ALWAYS)
====================================================================

Any use, copy, modification, or distribution of the Software, in
whole or in part, for Personal, Educational, or Commercial Use, must:

  (a) Include the following attribution in the README, documentation,
      footer, or another reasonably visible user-facing location:

        Based on Frakment by hanshapd
        https://github.com/hanshapd/frakment

  (b) Include this LICENSE file unmodified in all copies and
      derivative works.

  (c) Clearly mark any modified versions as modified, with a brief
      description of the changes (e.g., in a CHANGELOG or README).

====================================================================
4. CONTRIBUTION REQUIREMENT (COMMERCIAL USE ONLY)
====================================================================

Before using the Software for any Commercial Use, you (or the legal
entity you represent) must satisfy exactly ONE of the following
qualifying contributions. No more than one is required.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4.1  QUALIFYING CONTRIBUTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------

(a)  ONE MERGED PULL REQUEST

     A pull request that has been merged into the main branch of
     github.com/hanshapd/frakment, where all of the following are
     true:

       - The commit author is you (your GitHub username or email is
         recorded in the commit metadata).
       - The pull request makes at least one substantive change:
         fixes a bug, adds a feature, adds or corrects documentation,
         adds a test, translates content, or fixes a typo.
       - The pull request has not been reverted within 30 days of
         being merged.

     There is no minimum number of lines changed. A single-line
     typo fix qualifies. A documentation clarification qualifies.
     A test addition qualifies.

     A pull request that was closed without merging does NOT
     qualify. A pull request that was merged and later reverted
     within 30 days does NOT qualify.

(b)  ONE PAID SPONSORSHIP

     A single paid sponsorship transaction through the official
     GitHub Sponsors page for hanshapd, of any amount from USD 1
     upward. You must retain the receipt or the transaction ID
     issued by GitHub Sponsors.

(c)  WRITTEN PERMISSION

     A written statement from hanshapd - in a GitHub issue, a
     GitHub discussion, or a direct message on GitHub - that
     explicitly authorizes your commercial use of the Software
     and names Frakment. Verbal permission does NOT qualify. The
     statement must be in writing and must be retrievable by
     hanshapd on request.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4.2  SCOPE OF SATISFACTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Once a qualifying contribution under 4.1(a), (b), or (c) has been
made, the contribution requirement is satisfied permanently for:

  - the individual who made the contribution, OR
  - the legal entity (company, organization, or team) on whose
    behalf the contribution was made,

for all future Commercial Use of the Software by that individual
or entity. No further contributions are required for future
commercial use by the same party.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4.3  EVIDENCE ON REQUEST
--------------------------------------------------------------------

If hanshapd requests proof that the contribution requirement has
been satisfied, you must provide, within 30 days:

  - For 4.1(a): a link to the merged pull request on GitHub.
  - For 4.1(b): the sponsorship receipt or transaction ID.
  - For 4.1(c): a link or screenshot of the written permission.

Refusal or failure to provide evidence on request voids the
permission for Commercial Use until evidence is provided.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4.4  NO CONTRIBUTION REQUIRED FOR NON-COMMERCIAL USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Personal Use and Educational Use do NOT require any contribution.
Attribution (Section 3) is the only requirement for those uses.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4.5  ALTERNATIVE ARRANGEMENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------

If you cannot or do not wish to contribute, and you still want to
use the Software for Commercial Use, contact hanshapd on GitHub
(https://github.com/hanshapd) to arrange an alternative license.

